phantomfleet began as the `fake_news` load-testing tool that ships with
osctrl, written by Javier Marcos de Prado to simulate osquery nodes talking to
osctrl-tls. Huntbase Ltd extended it and extracted it into this
standalone project. The node simulation, enrollment and request loops,
latency statistics and output modes trace back to that tool.

Huntbase Ltd added, among other things: synthetic answers to arbitrary
distributed queries generated from the embedded osquery schema, per-platform
seed data and per-table row counts, heuristic SQL decomposition (`--explain`),
pinned node identities with deterministic UUIDs and cross-table consistency
(`--nodes-file`), support for non-osctrl servers (`--flavor generic`), and the
fictional Example Corp sample fleet.

